    usage: ["Defining options: You can define options as an array of objects or as the children of a component. The first approach is useful for cases where options require complex preparation and, possibly, memorization. The second one is convenient when there are few options, and their configuration does not require complex ca...","Storing data in options: You can define and store unique data in each option by using the option.data property. This can be useful when you need to enrich the data when using the onUpdate callback or, for example, when drawing your options with renderOption.","Selecting multiple options: To enable multiple selection, use the multiple property. Its default value is false.","Counter: You can add a counter of the selected items to the component using the hasCounter property.","Filtering options: To enable filter section, use the filterable property. Its default value is false.","Size: To manage the default control and option size, use the size property. Its default size is m.","Control width: By default, the control width stretches to match the width of the content of the selected options. You can manage it by using the width property: 'max': Stretches to the full width of the parent. number: Applies width in pixels.","Popup width: You can manage the popup width with the popupWidth property. The available values are: 'fit': Apply control width. number: Apply width in pixels."],
    propDescriptions: {"className":"Control className","defaultValue":"Default values that represent selected options in case of using an uncontrolled state","disabled":"Shows that the user cannot work with the control","filterable":"Shows that select popup has a filter section","filterOption":"Used to compare option with filter","filterPlaceholder":"Default filter input placeholder text","getOptionHeight":"Used to set height of customized user options","getOptionGroupHeight":"Used to set height of customized user option group","hasClear":"Enables displaying icon for clearing selected options","id":"id HTML attribute","label":"Control label","loading":"Adds the loading item to the end of the option list. Works like a persistent loading indicator while the options list is empty.","multiple":"Shows whether multiple options can be selected in the list","name":"Name of the control","onBlur":"Handler that is called when the element loses focus.","filter":"Controlled filter value","onFilterChange":"Fires every time after changing the filter","onFocus":"Handler that is called when the element gets focus","onLoadMore":"Fires when the loading indicator gets visible","onOpenChange":"Fires every time after changing popup visibility","onUpdate":"Fires when an alteration to the Select value is committed by the user","options":"Options to select","pin":"Control border view","placeholder":"Placeholder text","popupClassName":"Popup with the option list className","popupPlacement":"Popup placement","popupWidth":"Popup width","qa":"Test id attribute (data-qa)","renderControl":"Used to render user control","renderCounter":"Used to render user counter. Works only with hasCounter.","renderEmptyOptions":"Used to render a node for an empty option list","renderFilter":"Used to render user filter section","renderOption":"Used to render user options","renderOptionGroup":"Used to render user option groups","renderSelectedOption":"Used to render user selected options","renderPopup":"Used to render options list content","size":"Control / options size","value":"Values that represent selected options","view":"Control view","virtualizationThreshold":"Option count threshold after which virtualization is enabled","width":"Control width","errorMessage":"Error text","errorPlacement":"Error position","validationState":"Validation state","hasCounter":"Shows the selected option count. The counter appears only when the multiple selection is enabled."},
